      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under dry argon using Schlenk and vacuum-line techniques, 2 mL of trifluoroacetic acid was added to 30 mL of methanol containing 1.00 g (3.2 mmol) lanthanum(III) acetate and 2.15 mL (6.3 mmol) titanium(IV) butoxide. After stirring for 6 h a clear solution formed, which was evacuated to a dry solid and redissolved in 5 mL THF. The light-yellow concentrated solution was cannula-filtered into an evacuated glass vial and left at room temperature in a fume hood. Needle-like crystals of 1 formed after 28 days and were collected from the mother liquor (75% yield; mp 95 °C).",
